# Lab 4 – Automated IAM User Provisioning & RBAC

## Project Overview
This lab focuses on Identity and Access Management (IAM) user provisioning and role-based access control using Active Directory and PowerShell in a simulated corporate environment.

## Lab Environment
- Windows Server 2022
- Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)
- Windows PowerShell
- VMware Workstation Player
- Domain: jmc-local
- Domain Controller: JMC-DC01

## Objectives
- Explore automated user provisioning using PowerShell.
- Manage Active Directory user accounts.
- Apply role-based access control (RBAC).
- Review security group membership.
- Support least-privilege access management.

## IAM Workflow
1. Identify the user and their assigned organizational role.
2. Determine the appropriate Active Directory security group.
3. Provision or update the user account using PowerShell.
4. Assign access through role-based security groups.
5. Verify account attributes and group membership.
6. Document the results for auditing.

## Security Concepts
- Identity Lifecycle Management
- User Provisioning
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
- Least Privilege
- PowerShell Automation
- Access Verification

## Results
This project documents a lab workflow for provisioning and managing identities through Active Directory and PowerShell. Automation execution and specific access assignments will be supported by lab screenshots or script output.

